   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Zhian<div><br></div><div>I am using poppr v. 2.0.2.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;d like to generate a tree based on Nei&#39;s genetic distances.</div><div><br></div><div>I can do this as per the manual on all individuals. </div><div><div><br></div><div>aboot(a,cutoff = 70, tree=&quot;nj&quot;,quiet = TRUE, sample = 1000, distance = nei.dist)<br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div>But I want to do this between populations, I tried using the &quot;strata&quot; option here but it didn&#39;t work.<br></div><div><br></div><div>aboot(a,strata = ~METAPOP2, cutoff = 70, tree=&quot;nj&quot;,quiet = TRUE, sample = 1000, distance = nei.dist)<br></div></div><div><br></div><div>Is there a way to do this from within poppr?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Monique</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "wOXuSUQsBAAJ",
   "from": "Zhian Kamvar",
   "author": "d192ec4b1d416345",
   "date": "2015-08-19T16:20:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: nei distance using populations",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Monique<div><br></div><div>To generate a tree among populations, simply convert your genind to a genpop object. You can find an example in the &quot;Population Structure&quot; chapter in our Population Genetics in R manual:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Pop_Structure.html#genetic-distance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Pop_Structure.html%23genetic-distance&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480913813000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3IIBO3PzBe5xRsXtcdnnit\">http://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Pop_Structure.html#genetic-distance</a></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\"># Setup</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;poppr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;magrittr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># for the %&gt;% &quot;pipe&quot; operator</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;microbov&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>strata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">microbov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">other</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">microbov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>nameStrata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">microbov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Country</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Breed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Species</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Analysis</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">999</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>microbov </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  genind2genpop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pop </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Country</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Breed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  aboot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cutoff </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> quiet </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> distance </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nei</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>aboot doesn&#39;t have a strata argument specifically, but it&#39;s a good idea to have one as a signal to convert to a genpop object. I&#39;ll add it in the next version.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Zhian</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Wednesday, August 19, 2015 at 7:17:54 AM UTC-7, Monique Sakalidis wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Zhian<div><br></div><div>I am using poppr v. 2.0.2.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;d like to generate a tree based on Nei&#39;s genetic distances.</div><div><br></div><div>I can do this as per the manual on all individuals. </div><div><div><br></div><div>aboot(a,cutoff = 70, tree=&quot;nj&quot;,quiet = TRUE, sample = 1000, distance = nei.dist)<br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div>But I want to do this between populations, I tried using the &quot;strata&quot; option here but it didn&#39;t work.<br></div><div><br></div><div>aboot(a,strata = ~METAPOP2, cutoff = 70, tree=&quot;nj&quot;,quiet = TRUE, sample = 1000, distance = nei.dist)<br></div></div><div><br></div><div>Is there a way to do this from within poppr?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Monique</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
