r:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">other</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">microbov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>nameStrata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">microbov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Country</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Breed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Species</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Analysis</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">999</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>microbov </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  genind2genpop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pop </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Country</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Breed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  aboot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cutoff </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> quiet </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> distance </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nei</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>aboot doesn&#39;t have a strata argument specifically, but it&#39;s a good idea to have one as a signal to convert to a genpop object. I&#39;ll add it in the next version.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Zhian</div><br>On Wednesday, August 19, 2015 at 7:17:54 AM UTC-7, Monique Sakalidis wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Zhian<div><br></div><div>I am using poppr v. 2.0.2.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;d like to generate a tree based on Nei&#39;s genetic distances.</div><div><br></div><div>I can do this as per the manual on all individuals. </div><div><div><br></div><div>aboot(a,cutoff = 70, tree=&quot;nj&quot;,quiet = TRUE, sample = 1000, distance = nei.dist)<br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div>But I want to do this between populations, I tried using the &quot;strata&quot; option here but it didn&#39;t work.<br></div><div><br></div><div>aboot(a,strata = ~METAPOP2, cutoff = 70, tree=&quot;nj&quot;,quiet = TRUE, sample = 1000, distance = nei.dist)<br></div></div><div><br></div><div>Is there a way to do this from within poppr?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div><div>Monique</div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
